      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The authors extend graded semantics beyond finite-depth equivalence, prove an infinite-game characterization through algebraic quotients and coalgebra maps, and construct a final coalgebra from infinite-depth terms modulo the winning relation. The source supplies substantial local-presentability/accessibility arguments and complete nonadjacent infinite-game/finality proofs. These related infinite-depth goals are retained as one H2 framework result, preserving kappa-ary, terminal-object and monomorphism assumptions rather than counting support or case studies.",
